  "content": "Project name convention: display as **Yul'lu** (with apostrophe and capital Y); identifiers as **yullu** (lowercase, no apostrophe). The apostrophe can't survive in binary names, env vars (YULLU_*), file paths (.yullu/, ~/.local/share/yullu/), Go module path (github.com/tomanagle/yullu), domain (yullu.ai), MCP server name, or CSS class names. Use \"Yul'lu\" in every other human-readable place: READMEs, page titles, log banners, UI labels, marketing. Why: Yul'lu is a Butchella (Badtjala) word for bottlenose dolphins, chosen for the memory metaphor (dolphins recognise pod-mate signature whistles decades later). Acknowledged in README footer; if going commercial, reach out to the Butchella Aboriginal Corporation.\u003c/content\u003e\n\u003ctags\u003e[\"naming\", \"branding\"]\u003c/tags\u003e",
